<dialog id="how-dialog" class="info-dialog" aria-labelledby="how-title">
  <div class="dialog-heading"><h2 id="how-title">How it works</h2><button type="button" data-close-dialog aria-label="Close How it works">Close</button></div>
  <p class="dialog-intro">A model, not a crystal ball.</p>
  <div class="method-columns">
      <div>
        <h3>Start with the market</h3><p>
          Daily snapshots are refreshed when this site is built. They contain
          completed Yahoo Finance candles; stock prices are adjusted.
          Observation and fetch dates stay visible. These are daily
          observations, not live quotes.
        </p>
      </div><div>
        <h3>Let Kronos find a path</h3><p>
          Kronos runs on your device using up to 256 candles of context. Three
          sampled paths are averaged into the closing prices and volumes you see. Volume estimates below zero are displayed as zero. Results
          can vary between runs.
        </p>
      </div><div>
        <h3>Keep the uncertainty</h3><p>
          A forecast is an estimate, not a guarantee or a confidence interval.
          Use this as a research tool, alongside your own judgment.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  <p class="dialog-note">For research only. Not financial advice.</p>
</dialog>
<dialog id="about-dialog" class="info-dialog" aria-labelledby="about-title">
  <div class="dialog-heading"><h2 id="about-title">About Stock Predictor</h2><button type="button" data-close-dialog aria-label="Close About">Close</button></div>
  <p class="dialog-intro">A workspace for exploring daily market forecasts.</p>
  <p>Explore stocks, ETFs and cryptocurrency using Kronos models that run on your device. Published snapshots load first; forecasts are generated when you request them.</p>
  <p>Your selections are remembered in this browser. Remove downloaded model files through Settings in the navbar.</p>
  <p>CPU is the default. GPU uses WebGPU where supported; if a forecast fails, switch to CPU and try again. Larger models need more memory.</p>
  <a href="https://github.com/statickidz/stock-predictor" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View the project on GitHub</a>
  <p class="dialog-note">For research only. Not financial advice.</p>
</dialog>

<dialog id="disclaimer-dialog" class="info-dialog" aria-labelledby="disclaimer-title">
  <div class="dialog-heading"><h2 id="disclaimer-title">Disclaimer</h2><button type="button" data-close-dialog aria-label="Close Disclaimer">Close</button></div>
  <p class="dialog-intro">For research and education only.</p>
  <p>Stock Predictor does not provide financial advice or recommendations to buy, sell or hold an asset.</p>
  <p>Model forecasts are estimates, can vary between runs and may be wrong. They do not guarantee future prices or trading volumes and do not represent calibrated confidence intervals.</p>
  <p>Market data consists of daily snapshots, not live quotes. Check the observation and fetch dates shown with each asset; snapshots may be out of date.</p>
  <p>Use your own judgment and independent research when making financial decisions. Investing involves risk, including the loss of capital.</p>
</dialog>
